A||N||3||Vlad||Jacobs Coil vs. MSD Blaster||||1||
Z||000000||Vlad||05-18-2001||07:26 PM||||Hello,<P>I'm thinking about making a little upgrade to my GT. <BR>What advantage could I achive by replacing the original 15 years old coil using one of the aftermarket products? Should I consider this replacment at all provided that the old coil is still working?<P>Also, does anybody have an experience using those products? How are they?<P>The cost of MSD Blaster here is $57 Can,<BR>and Jacobs  - $37 Can.<P>So now I have a dilema what to choose....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||05-18-2001||07:45 PM|||| I have the Jacobs omni pak. Thats the whole ignition. I love it. They quoted me the hp and milage gains and after tuning I got them. As for the coil by itself, I don't know.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||05-18-2001||09:39 PM||||I would spend the money on the MSD coil. I got the Accel coil and my ass-o-meter says that at higher RPM the engine has more pull.<P>You may gain 1 horsepower but mostly what you will gain is more complete high rpm combustion and better gas mileage. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 05-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Vlad||05-18-2001||09:45 PM||||I guess even if the only benefit is a better gas mileage, the coil already worths its money.<P>||||reg||1
